WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:01.701
 All right, bladesmiths.

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:03.269
Congratulations.

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:04.637
The two of you have made it
through the first two rounds

00:00:04.738 --> 00:00:06.272
of our [inaudible]
competition, which means you're

00:00:06.372 --> 00:00:07.707
going into the final round.

00:00:07.774 --> 00:00:10.043
Now we are giving you four
days at your home forges

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:12.044
to battle it out for the
title of "Forged in Fire"

00:00:12.145 --> 00:00:15.648
champion and a
check for $10,000.

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:17.517
We want you to build this--

00:00:21.186 --> 00:00:25.191
the Mesopotamian sickle sword.

00:00:25.258 --> 00:00:27.459
The sickle sword
originated in Mesopotamia

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:31.363
at the height of the
Bronze Age, around 2500 BC.

00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:33.299
These sickle and
curve-shaped swords

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:35.568
often symbolized
royalty and power,

00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:38.004
and were primarily
wielded during ceremonies

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:39.772
by kings and authority figures.

00:00:39.839 --> 00:00:42.308
Although these swords were
not common on the battlefield,

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:45.444
the belly of the blade allowed
for quick, devastating blows,

00:00:45.511 --> 00:00:47.379
and inspired designs
for later weapons,

00:00:47.479 --> 00:00:49.949
such as the deadly
Egyptian khopesh.

00:00:50.016 --> 00:00:51.017
Good luck.

00:00:51.083 --> 00:00:52.952
We will see you in four days.

00:00:53.019 --> 00:00:53.787
 Go.

00:00:58.024 --> 00:00:59.692 line:14%
 My name's Robert Taylor.

00:00:59.792 --> 00:01:01.527 line:14%
I'm from Brentwood, California.

00:01:01.627 --> 00:01:04.396
I'm a sergeant with the San
Francisco Sheriff's Department.

00:01:04.496 --> 00:01:06.032
I took up bladesmithing
because I liked

00:01:06.099 --> 00:01:07.366
watching "Forged in Fire."

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:09.501
It was something I really
wanted to go further in,

00:01:09.568 --> 00:01:11.837
become an ABS smith,
maybe a master smith

00:01:11.937 --> 00:01:13.472
someday, because I love forging.

00:01:13.539 --> 00:01:15.608
So I'm going to go
500 layers of Damascus

00:01:15.675 --> 00:01:18.411
on each side with
a 1084 center core.

00:01:18.478 --> 00:01:20.412
All right, we're going
for our final forge weld.

00:01:20.479 --> 00:01:22.281
As long as I'm
solid with my steel,

00:01:22.381 --> 00:01:24.584
1084 will give it a
more stronger center.

00:01:24.684 --> 00:01:26.486
The place where I want
to bend will bend down,

00:01:26.553 --> 00:01:27.787
and then the tip
will start bending

00:01:27.853 --> 00:01:29.155
up automatically as I hit it.

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:30.789
ROBERT (VOICEOVER): I'm
whacking it on the horn

00:01:30.856 --> 00:01:31.857
to get it to bend down.

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:34.360
It's easier than
using the hammer.

00:01:34.427 --> 00:01:35.361
 I like it.

00:01:35.427 --> 00:01:36.796
Got the bilt all
ready for the quench.

00:01:36.863 --> 00:01:38.297
ROBERT (VOICEOVER): If this
quench doesn't go right,

00:01:38.397 --> 00:01:39.565
I'm gonna have to go
ahead and start over.

00:01:39.665 --> 00:01:40.467
And that's gonna suck.

00:01:43.703 --> 00:01:45.371
Went in pretty hot.

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:48.908
We'll see if we have
any bad forge welds.

00:01:48.975 --> 00:01:50.309
We have a hard lake.

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:52.278
 I want to keep it light
enough and balanced enough

00:01:52.345 --> 00:01:53.880
for somebody to swing it.

00:01:53.947 --> 00:01:54.947
Getting there.

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:57.717
Feel really good
about my weapon.

00:01:57.817 --> 00:01:59.251
Getting all the fit-up done.

00:01:59.351 --> 00:02:01.521
I think this thing's gonna slice
anything they put before it.

00:02:07.226 --> 00:02:08.728 line:14%
 My name is Jacob Gates.

00:02:08.794 --> 00:02:11.931 line:8%
I am 20 years old, and I'm
from Royalton, Minnesota.

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:15.100
Martial arts has always been
my first love and first hobby.

00:02:15.167 --> 00:02:16.902
And then I got
into bladesmithing.

00:02:17.003 --> 00:02:18.370
JACOB (VOICEOVER):
They both kind

00:02:18.437 --> 00:02:20.205
of crisscross, because
when you're making a knife,

00:02:20.305 --> 00:02:22.708
it's just got to be
real patient with it.

00:02:22.775 --> 00:02:24.243
Wax on, wax off.

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:26.645 line:8%
I'm gonna put a ladder
pattern in this steel.

00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:29.348
Kinda can see the ladder
pattern in there already.

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:30.683
 The length and
curve of this blade

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:32.385
is gonna be difficult
to work with just

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:34.253
because I want to make sure
everything stays straight

00:02:34.353 --> 00:02:36.622
and doesn't have
any warps to it.

00:02:36.689 --> 00:02:37.523
Looking good so far.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:38.925
Because ultimately,
that could send

00:02:38.991 --> 00:02:40.259
me home if that's not spot-on.

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:42.094
We're getting ready
to quench here.

00:02:42.194 --> 00:02:43.829
I feel pretty good
about my progress.

00:02:43.896 --> 00:02:45.765
Everything looks good.

00:02:45.865 --> 00:02:47.367
That's a good temperature.

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:51.904
Oh, that is straight.

00:02:52.004 --> 00:02:53.071
Everything's looking good.

00:02:53.172 --> 00:02:54.440 line:8%
Now we're gonna
have to temper it.

00:02:54.507 --> 00:02:56.375 line:8%
That's gonna take away a
little of this hardness

00:02:56.475 --> 00:02:58.177 line:8%
and it's gonna' add
toughness, because right

00:02:58.277 --> 00:02:59.478
now, it's pretty brittle.

00:02:59.578 --> 00:03:00.946
If I just went and
smacked it on my anvil,

00:03:01.013 --> 00:03:02.114
it would probably shatter.

00:03:02.181 --> 00:03:03.149
I think the hardest
part is gonna

00:03:03.215 --> 00:03:04.450
be getting the heat just right.

00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:05.985
I don't have an oven
long enough to fit

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:09.122
this sword in so we're gonna
have to do it all with a torch.

00:03:09.189 --> 00:03:12.191
It's not going to be as
precise as having an oven.

00:03:12.291 --> 00:03:13.559
Don't want to overheat it.

00:03:13.659 --> 00:03:15.328
Makes me a little bit
nervous because I don't

00:03:15.428 --> 00:03:16.529
know the ultimate outcome.

00:03:16.595 --> 00:03:18.198
But hopefully, we
get it just right.

00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:19.899
I want to make sure everything
is even on this handle

00:03:19.966 --> 00:03:22.001
and everything feels good.

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:23.703
The martial artists,
they're really into flow

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:24.904
and I'm really into feel.

00:03:25.004 --> 00:03:26.406
Feels good.

00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:28.074
I'm not quite sure what my
strength test is gonna be.

00:03:28.141 --> 00:03:29.508
But I think whatever
they throw at it,

00:03:29.608 --> 00:03:31.076
it's gonna be able to handle it.

00:03:31.143 --> 00:03:34.680
 Bladesmiths, welcome
to the kill test.

00:03:34.747 --> 00:03:37.383
So to find out what kind of
lethal damage they will do,

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:40.052
I'm gonna take your weapons,
deliver some lethal blows

00:03:40.119 --> 00:03:42.121
to this ballistics dummy.

00:03:42.221 --> 00:03:43.188
Jacob, you're up first.
Ready?

00:03:43.288 --> 00:03:44.257
 Cut the head off.

00:03:44.324 --> 00:03:45.024
 Let's do that.

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:48.628
[music playing]

00:04:11.317 --> 00:04:12.919
 [laughs]

00:04:15.320 --> 00:04:16.522
 All right, Jacob.

00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:18.891
Let's talk about your
sickle sword right here.

00:04:18.958 --> 00:04:21.394
Your edge is razor sharp.

00:04:21.461 --> 00:04:23.896
Coupled with the fact that
this is a very light weapon,

00:04:23.963 --> 00:04:28.200
I can use velocity to really
wield that sharp edge.

00:04:28.267 --> 00:04:30.669
It cuts deep into
this ballistics dummy.

00:04:30.736 --> 00:04:34.974
And overall, sir, your
weapon, it will kill.

00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:36.142
 Thank you.

00:04:36.209 --> 00:04:37.143
 All right, Robert.

00:04:37.243 --> 00:04:38.076
Your turn, sir.
You ready?

00:04:38.143 --> 00:04:38.977
 I'm ready.

00:04:39.044 --> 00:04:39.712
 Right.

00:04:39.779 --> 00:04:40.947
Let's do this.

00:04:41.014 --> 00:04:43.950
[music playing]

00:05:05.971 --> 00:05:08.374
All right, Robert, let's
talk about your sickle sword.

00:05:08.441 --> 00:05:10.810
It's a very light
blade, that much

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:11.978
lighter than the other one.

00:05:12.045 --> 00:05:14.113
And the angle that
you have in here

00:05:14.213 --> 00:05:16.015
lends itself to use
not only velocity,

00:05:16.082 --> 00:05:19.251
but the sharpness of your
edge to cut very deep

00:05:19.318 --> 00:05:21.220
into this ballistics dummy.

00:05:21.286 --> 00:05:23.855
And overall, sir, it will kill.

00:05:23.922 --> 00:05:24.991
 Thank you.

00:05:29.028 --> 00:05:31.831
 Bladesmiths, welcome
to the strength test,

00:05:31.898 --> 00:05:33.566
the armored warrior chop.

00:05:33.666 --> 00:05:36.736
To test the strength and overall
durability of your Mesopotamian

00:05:36.802 --> 00:05:39.271
sickle swords, I'm
gonna be chopping

00:05:39.338 --> 00:05:41.406
into these armored warriors.

00:05:41.506 --> 00:05:42.909
Jacob, you're up first.
You ready for this?

00:05:42.975 --> 00:05:43.976
 I don't think I get a choice.

00:05:44.043 --> 00:05:46.979
 You don't have a choice.

00:05:47.046 --> 00:05:50.016
[music playing]

00:06:25.117 --> 00:06:27.953
What actually happened is your
sword bit into the other sword

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:31.090
by about 3/16 of an inch
and it took out this chip.

00:06:31.157 --> 00:06:35.127
And once that chip was gone,
the whole sword blew up.

00:06:35.227 --> 00:06:36.729
Your grain looks good.

00:06:36.795 --> 00:06:41.233
But unfortunately, it's just
this sword against that sword.

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:42.201
This time, that sword won.

00:06:42.301 --> 00:06:43.069
 Yep.

00:06:47.006 --> 00:06:49.508
 All right, Jacob, we
hate to see this happen.

00:06:49.574 --> 00:06:51.043
You gave us a beautiful blade.

00:06:51.143 --> 00:06:53.612
But unfortunately, it did
suffer catastrophic failure

00:06:53.679 --> 00:06:55.214
on the seventh strike.

00:06:55.314 --> 00:06:56.915
But you are not out
of the fight yet,

00:06:56.982 --> 00:06:58.817
because Robert, in order
to become the champion,

00:06:58.884 --> 00:07:02.054
you will have to survive every
single one of those seven

00:07:02.154 --> 00:07:03.823
strikes on the armored warrior.

00:07:03.890 --> 00:07:04.490
Are you ready?

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:05.357
 Let's roll the dice.

00:07:05.458 --> 00:07:07.993
 All right, Ben.

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:12.665
[music playing]

00:07:39.759 --> 00:07:42.695
Well, Robert, the big
thing is it's one sword.

00:07:42.762 --> 00:07:43.261
Nice job.

00:07:43.328 --> 00:07:46.498
 Thank you.

00:07:46.565 --> 00:07:49.535
 Well, Robert, you made
it through all the testing.

00:07:49.601 --> 00:07:51.504
Jacob, it's a beautiful
piece of work.

00:07:51.571 --> 00:07:53.339
Unfortunately, due to
your catastrophic failure,

00:07:53.439 --> 00:07:54.873
we cannot continue testing.

00:07:54.940 --> 00:07:56.575
And for that reason, I'm gonna
have to ask you to please

00:07:56.642 --> 00:07:57.610
step off the forge floor.

00:07:57.710 --> 00:07:58.744
 Thank you, gentlemen.

00:07:58.845 --> 00:07:59.411
It was an honor.

00:07:59.511 --> 00:08:00.546
 Thank you very much.

00:08:00.613 --> 00:08:01.880
 Very nice job.

00:08:01.947 --> 00:08:04.016
 Thank you.

00:08:04.083 --> 00:08:06.585
 You know, it totally sucks.

00:08:06.652 --> 00:08:08.921
JACOB (VOICEOVER): But I
really am proud of the blade

00:08:09.021 --> 00:08:10.222
I made either way.

00:08:10.289 --> 00:08:12.524
 You know, they said pretty
much nothing but good things

00:08:12.624 --> 00:08:13.792
about it, up until it broke.

00:08:13.892 --> 00:08:15.861
And, well, I'd totally
come back for this

00:08:15.961 --> 00:08:20.098
and maybe get a shot at
making it all the way through.

00:08:20.165 --> 00:08:23.102
 Robert, we never like to
see competitors' blades break.

00:08:23.169 --> 00:08:25.972
But yours did not, and
that makes you the newest

00:08:26.072 --> 00:08:27.073
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:08:27.139 --> 00:08:29.909
You just got yourself
a check for $10,000.

00:08:29.976 --> 00:08:30.576
Congratulations.

00:08:30.643 --> 00:08:31.777
 Thanks.
[applause]

00:08:31.877 --> 00:08:32.377
Thanks.

00:08:32.477 --> 00:08:33.445
 Feel pretty good?

00:08:33.546 --> 00:08:34.647
 Crazy, dude.

00:08:34.747 --> 00:08:35.214
Crazy.

00:08:35.281 --> 00:08:36.715
[laughter]

00:08:36.782 --> 00:08:37.816
ROBERT (VOICEOVER): Winning
this championship, I think,

00:08:37.917 --> 00:08:39.852
has really pushed
me to my limits.

00:08:39.952 --> 00:08:41.853
And then that makes me want
to push them even more.

00:08:41.920 --> 00:08:43.289
Now that I'm a
champion, I'm gonna

00:08:43.389 --> 00:08:45.457
go ahead and get my
ABS Smith membership

00:08:45.524 --> 00:08:48.160
and just really
refine my skills.

